# The Great Pumpkin Pie

Based on [Sally’s Baking Addiction](https://sallysbakingaddiction.com/the-great-pumpkin-pie-recipe)

{ rating="0" image="None" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

### Sugared Cranberries

- [ ] 1 cup (100g) fresh [cranberries]{ ing="cranberries" }
- [ ] 3/4 cup (180ml) [water]{ ing="water" }
- [ ] 1.25 cups (250g) [granulated sugar]{ ing="granulated-sugar" }, divided (3/4 cup for syrup, 1/2 cup for coating)

### Pie Crust

- [ ] [Homemade pie dough]{ ing="homemade-pie-dough" } (makes 2 crusts) or store-bought
- [ ] 1 large [egg beaten]{ ing="egg-beaten" } with 1 Tbsp milk (egg wash)

### Filling

- [ ] One 15-ounce can (425g) [pumpkin puree]{ ing="pumpkin-puree" }
- [ ] 3 large [eggs]{ ing="egg" }
- [ ] 1.25 cups (250g) packed [light or dark brown sugar]{ ing="brown-sugar" }
- [ ] 1 Tbsp (8g) [cornstarch]{ ing="cornstarch" }
- [ ] 1/2 tsp [salt]{ ing="salt" }
- [ ] 1.5 tsp [ground cinnamon]{ ing="ground-cinnamon" }
- [ ] 1/2 tsp [ground ginger]{ ing="ground-ginger" }
- [ ] 1/4 tsp ground or [freshly grated nutmeg]{ ing="freshly-grated-nutmeg" }
- [ ] 1/8 tsp [ground cloves]{ ing="ground-cloves" }
- [ ] 1/8 tsp fresh [ground black pepper]{ ing="ground-black-pepper" }
- [ ] 1 cup (240ml) [heavy cream]{ ing="heavy-cream" }
- [ ] 1/4 cup (60ml) [milk]{ ing="milk" }

## Recipe

1. Prepare sugared [cranberries]{ ing="cranberries" } (overnight recommended): Bring [water]{ ing="water" } and 3/4 cup [sugar]{ ing="granulated-sugar" } to simmer, dissolve sugar, cool 5 minutes, pour over cranberries, let sit 15 minutes covered. Spread on parchment to dry 1 hour, toss in remaining 1/2 cup sugar, dry uncovered at least 1 hour
1. Prepare pie crust through step 5 per [pie dough]{ ing="homemade-pie-dough" } instructions or use store-bought
1. Preheat oven to 375F (190C)
1. Roll chilled [dough]{ ing="homemade-pie-dough" } into 12-inch circle on floured surface, place in 9x2-inch deep dish pie pan, tuck and crimp edges, brush with [egg]{ ing="egg" } wash
1. Par-bake: Line with parchment and pie weights, bake 10 minutes, remove weights, prick bottom with fork, bake 7-8 more minutes until bottom just starts browning
1. Whisk together pumpkin, 3 [eggs]{ ing="egg" }, and [brown sugar]{ ing="brown-sugar" } until combined. Add [cornstarch]{ ing="cornstarch" }, [salt]{ ing="salt" }, spices, [pepper]{ ing="ground-black-pepper" }, [heavy cream]{ ing="heavy-cream" }, and [milk]{ ing="milk" }. Whisk vigorously
1. Pour filling into warm crust (about 3/4 full), bake 55-60 minutes until center is almost set with slight wobble in middle. Cover crust edges with foil after 25 minutes
1. Cool on wire rack completely for at least 3 hours
1. Decorate with sugared [cranberries]{ ing="cranberries" } and pie crust leaves, serve with whipped [cream]{ ing="heavy-cream" }

## Notes

- Serves 8-10
- Yields approximately 1 cup sugared cranberries
- Pie crust leaves are optional decoration
- Some leftover filling may remain; use scraps for mini pies
- Store covered in refrigerator up to 5 days
